Create a professional BPMN-style process modeling application using only HTML, CSS, SVG, and vanilla JavaScript (no external dependencies).

Requirements:

1. Use SVG as the rendering engine for all BPMN objects and connectors.

2. Support BPMN elements:
   
   - Start Event
   - End Event
   - Task
   - Sub-Process
   - Exclusive Gateway
   - Parallel Gateway
   - Swimlanes
   - Sequence Flows
   - Text Annotations

3. Implement an automatic layout engine that:
   
   - Prevents overlapping objects.
   - Automatically spaces elements horizontally and vertically.
   - Resizes swimlanes based on contained objects.
   - Supports long activity names and multi-line text.
   - Automatically adjusts object size according to content.
   - Maintains alignment across swimlanes.
   - Keeps a consistent grid-based structure.

4. Implement intelligent connector routing:
   
   - Use orthogonal (right-angle) connectors.
   - Avoid connectors crossing through objects.
   - Automatically reroute connectors when objects move.
   - Display professional BPMN arrowheads.
   - Minimize line crossings.

5. Implement collision detection:
   
   - Detect overlapping objects.
   - Automatically reposition objects when overlap occurs.
   - Maintain minimum spacing between all elements.

6. Make every BPMN element interactive:
   
   - Drag and drop.
   - Resize using handles.
   - Select and highlight.
   - Edit labels inline.
   - Delete objects.
   - Duplicate objects.

7. Provide a modern BPMN designer experience:
   
   - Zoom in/out.
   - Pan canvas.
   - Snap to grid.
   - Undo/redo.
   - Multi-select support.
   - Context menu actions.

8. Ensure labels are handled professionally:
   
   - Auto-wrap long text.
   - Dynamically increase object height when needed.
   - Keep text centered and readable.
   - Prevent text overflow.

9. Architecture:
   
   - Separate data model, layout engine, connector engine, and renderer.
   - Maintain all BPMN objects in JSON.
   - Re-render automatically after changes.
   - Support importing and exporting JSON.

10. Design goals:
    
    - Clean BPMN appearance similar to Signavio, Visio, Camunda Modeler, or BPMN.io.
    - Minimal visual clutter.
    - Professional spacing.
    - No overlapping objects.
    - No connector collisions.
    - Responsive layout.
    - Production-quality user experience.

Generate complete, well-structured, commented code with modular architecture and best practices. Prioritize automatic layout, collision avoidance, swimlane management, and professional connector routing over visual styling.